[ti:Day 14]

[00:00.00]hierarchy 例 The lady in red clothes is high up in the management hierarchy. 那位穿红色衣服的女士 在管理层中地位很高。
[00:09.16]secretarial 例 She could not afford to pay off the mortgage payment after losing her secretarial job. 丢掉秘书的工作后，她偿还不起抵押贷款。
[00:21.57]isolated 例 It is not an isolated business case. 这不是一 个孤立的商业案例。
[00:27.34]innovate 例 It's hard for us to innovate if there's a great difficulty in attracting investors. 如果很难吸引 到投资者，我们就难以创新。
[00:39.01]audience 例 If your audiences don't have an obvious reason to be interested, tell them why they should listen to you. 如果你的听众还没有明显发 现兴趣所在，就告诉他们为什么非要听你说不 可。
[00:53.20]inscrutable 例 It's one of the world's leading and somewhat inscrutable technology companies. 它是全球最顶尖也是最神秘的科技企业之一。
[01:05.02]merchandise 例 Under what circumstances can the distributor return merchandise to the manufacturer? 在什么情况下分销商能将商品返 还给制造商？
[01:17.73]frequency 例 If you want to save money and increase your productivity, you do well to reduce the number and frequency of such stupid decisions. 如果想节省开支、提高生产率，你最 好努力减少作这种愚蠢决定的数量和频率。
[01:35.17]apparent 例 In that case, the benchmark should be adjusted so that any further slowdown will become apparent the next time. 如果是这样的 话，基准就需要调整，这样之后任何的性能下降 都会显而易见。
[01:50.24]afloat 例 During the financial crisis, he had to sell his house to keep the business afloat. 金融危机期 间，他不得不卖掉自己的住房以确保企业免于负 债。
[02:01.33]embark 例 More and more people are embarking money to real estate to make a fortune. 越来 越多的人投资于房地产，期望着能发一笔财。
[02:11.38]abdicate 例 The people in Ireland, their children and even their grandchildren would have to pay off heavy debts if the government abdicated its responsibility to regulate and restrain the financial sector. 如果爱尔兰政府不履行其规范、 控制财政部门的职责，爱尔兰人民乃至他们的后 世子孙都将背负沉重的债务。
[02:37.09]plague 例 Worries about joblessness plague most of the workforce. 大部分雇员活在对失业的担心之 中。
[02:45.22]backfire 例 If history could live over, the President's proposal would backfire. 如果历史可以重来，总 统的提议可能会适得其反。
[02:55.27]consular 例 Both sides exchanged views on bilateral consular cooperation and other issues of common concern. 双方就双边领事合作等共同关 注的问题交换了看法。
[03:08.86]mould 例 The mould factory plans to expand the scale and product lines. 这家模具厂计划扩大规 模和增加产品线。
[03:17.43]debasement 例 Quantitative easing is supposed to be part of a general tendency towards the debasement of currencies. 量化宽松被认为是货 币贬值大趋势的一部分。
[03:31.92]ignite 例 It can ignite your fighting will. 它能点燃你的 斗志。
[03:37.09]auxiliary 例 Auxiliary storage devices will augment the memory capacity. 辅助存储设备可以加大内存容 量。
[03:46.25]recede 例 The price of my company's shares has receded now. 现在我公司的股价已经回跌。
[03:53.35]indemnity 例 The indemnity contract requires both sides to exercise the utmost faith. 该赔偿合同要求双 方当事人拿出最大的诚意。
[04:03.99]adjourn 例 The summit on financial crisis was adjourned for four days. 关于金融危机的峰会被 延期了四天。
[04:12.56]oversubscribe 例 The stock has been oversubscribed after its launch, so there has to be a ballot for the shares. 这只股票一经发行就被超额认购，因此只 好通过抽签来决定股票份额。
[04:26.15]undervalue 例 Never undervalue women's contribution to economic development. 永远不要低估女性对经 济发展所作的贡献。
[04:36.05]due 例 When does the bill fall due? 这个票据什么时 候到期？
[04:40.04]downturn 例 The worst downturn since the Great Depression is only part of the problem. 自经济 大萧条后，糟糕的经济衰退只是问题的一部分。
[04:50.54]foreman 例 The boss called the foreman on the carpet for granting sick leave to a worker without first asking for permission. 老板批评工头未事先 请示就擅自批准一个工人的病假。
[05:05.76]tag 例 Please tag every item in the store. 请给店里 的所有货品加上标签。
[05:10.64]damages 例 Tom is gathering evidence to claim for damages against the entities responsible for the injuries. 汤姆正在收集证据，向应对损害负责 的单位索要损害赔偿金。
[05:24.08]beware 例 The fire department urges the public to beware of winter blazes. 消防部门提醒公众要谨 防冬季火灾。
[05:33.10]collapse 例 The economy of this nation was brought into a state of disaster, and for a time even on the brink of collapse. 这个国家的经济被弄得百 孔千疮，甚至一度面临崩溃。
[05:47.58]epidemic 例 An unemployment epidemic is a result of economic crisis. 经济危机导致失业率猛增。
[05:56.01]applicable 例 This section of the law is applicable only to corporations. 这部分法律只适用于公司。
[06:05.02]average 例 In this simple case, customers are only described by age and average balance. 在这个 简单的案例中，客户只以年龄和平均余额来描 述。
[06:15.81]avow 例 The senator was forced to avow openly that he had received some money from that company. 那个参议员被迫承认曾经收过那家公司 的一些钱。
[06:27.34]encroachment 例 That's a sign of the encroachment of commercialism in education. 那是一种教育被商 业化侵蚀的征兆。
[06:37.38]slump 例 The authorities attributed the slump in retail business to increasing costs and the impact from online sales. 官方将零售业萧条的 原因归咎于成本增加及在线销售的影响。
[06:52.02]axe 例 The British government will cut investment spending and pensions and axe 10,000 publicsector jobs in a drive to meet EU deficit targets. 英国政府将减少投资、降低养老金并削 减一万个公共部门的职位，从而将赤字维持在欧 盟的标准之内。
[07:09.60]corporate 例 In Japan and Britain, corporate investment fell by about a quarter from peak to trough. 在 日本与英国，公司投资额从高峰下降了约四分之 一。
[07:21.87]feasible 例 To broaden the market in Europe seems feasible in theory but not in practice. 扩展欧洲 市场的想法在理论上似乎可行，但不够实际。
[07:32.66]autarky 例 Figures on the decline in world trade are horrible for anybody except anti-globalisation advocates of autarky. 世界贸易量下降的数据对 任何人而言都是可怕的，当然，反对全球化、倡 导自给自足的人除外。
[07:47.88]oversight 例 To facilitate the oversight process, the government requires related divisions to report back periodically on their activities. 为 了便于监督，政府要求相关部门定期汇报其活动 内容。
[08:05.76]accomplish 例 The engineers have accomplished the first part of the project. 工程师们已经完成了这个项 目的头期工程。
[08:15.22]establish 例 We have established a long-term relationship of cooperation after many years of effort. 经过多年的努力，我们建立了长期的合 作关系。
[08:27.78]loophole 例 He employed a lawyer to find loopholes in the purchase contract. 他聘请了一位律师来查 找购买合同中的漏洞。
